module sysl

// The two tables `shortest_decimal` multiplies by, each entry to 125 significant bits.
//
// `pow5_inv_split[q]` is `floor(2^j / 5^q) + 1` with `j = bitlength(5^q) - 1 + 125`, which scales a
// value down by 10^q once the power of two it leaves is shifted off. `pow5_split[i]` is `5^i` with
// its low bits dropped (or zeros appended) to leave exactly 125, which scales a value up. Both are
// Ryu's tables, generated with exact integer arithmetic; the sizes cover every exponent a finite
// double has.

